{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "fc", "rep": 220, "hyps": [{"edit_param": "alpha", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "alpha", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Increasing an already large L2 penalty causes severe underfitting, as seen in the 0.129->1 probe losing 6-11 pp on all datasets."}, {"edit_param": "alpha", "edit_dir": "down", "cond_param": "alpha", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "higher", "why": "Reducing alpha relieves over-regularization only when alpha is large; at small alpha the change is negligible."}, {"edit_param": "depth", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deeper ReLU nets trained with Adam at very high learning rates diverge or collapse, as in probes #97 and #52."}, {"edit_param": "depth", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "depth", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "higher", "why": "Going from 1 to 2 hidden layers adds meaningful nonlinearity (large phoneme gains), while 2 to 3 shows diminishing or negative returns."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "higher", "why": "With tiny learning rates the network is undertrained in 243 epochs, so increasing the rate helps a lot."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Raising an already large learning rate pushes Adam into instability and divergence."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "down", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "higher", "why": "Lowering a too-large learning rate recovers stable training, whereas lowering a moderate one just slows learning."}, {"edit_param": "batch_size", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "higher", "why": "Larger batches reduce gradient noise and stabilize training at high learning rat